WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.480
– Alan Walker, welcome!

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.360
You have spent a lot of
 time on stage.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.480
Do you sometimes get surprised
 of your own success?

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.160
– The thought strikes me just by
 watching these videoes.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.520
During the pandemic, I’ve had a
lot of time to look back on

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.520
old pictures and stuff like that

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.520
it’s like: "Wow, have I
 done all that?"

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.480
It feels weird

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.560
because everything has
 happened so quickly,

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.920
but it’s been a lot of fun.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.320
One of your first songs is
called "Fade".

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:45.920
– Yes.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.000
– How old were you when you
 made that song?

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.960
– 15-16 years old.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.720
– It became a big hit.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:55.640
And then I thought

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.760
can we get a masterclass

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.760
in how you build a song like that?

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.562
– Yes.

00:01:01.821 --> 00:01:04.101
– So I asked you to bring your
 computer.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:06.480
And then I thought ...

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.520
You should know that she is a
 DJ herself.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.320
She has worked as a DJ.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.280
Have you not?

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:14.880
– Yes, but I mean ...

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.200
– Yes, I have been a DJ,

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.280
but not with that kind
 of audience.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.240
– But you could ask relevant
 questions.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.720
– Absolutely! You could teach
 me how to produce.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.080
– How do you start to build
 a song like that?

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.200
– We can start with the basics.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.480
What I did when I started making
 the song ...

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.680
I didn’t have any knowledge
 of music production.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.680
I had produced music for
 two years.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.560
I made the song based
 on a gut feeling.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.400
When I started making the song

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.520
I started with
a four hit chord progression.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:01.880
Which is pretty standard

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.480
and you hear it in a lot 
of top songs nowadays.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.520
Something else I have
 found out when making          

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.560
is to not have the
 song in 128 bpm

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.880
which is a high tempo and
 very common.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.640
– Now you’re too technical.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.720
128 bpm, what is that?

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.000
– Beats per minute.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.080
– So, the rhythm?

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:25.260
– Yes.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.840
I decided to do something
different with the song

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.200
and slow down the tempo. 

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.960
I turned the tempo down
 to 90 bpm and found out

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:43.640
that you could hear the melodies
and the layers better,

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.440
I thought that sounded beautful.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.640
– Let us hear the start of
 the song.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.520
– Go into character. 

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.480
– It’s very simple.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:12.320
From the start of the song to 
the drop, its the same melody.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.120
– Do you see how
 easy it is, Fredrik?

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.000
– You make it seem very easy.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.960
– The most important thing
for me in the song

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.560
is that the melody tells
a story throughout the song.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.800
– So that’s what you’re adding?

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.920
– Now it’s just the same
 melody over and over again,

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.240
but it builds up.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:54.400
– And there it becomes "Fade".

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.680
– That’s the drop,

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.280
which is basically the chorus,
since it’s an instrumental song.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.080
– What fascinates me, is that
today there are probably

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.560
right now a lot of people
with great equipment

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.320
trying to create songs
like this. 

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.240
And then you create a song 

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.520
by using these four chords, that
have been used many times before.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.560
It’s like Picasso painting
 a dog,

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:19.360
it becomes perfect 
and you want to you hear it.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.720
– Then you do some small
 changes. 

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.880
Let’s hear it now and 
people will recognize it.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.880
– Yes it will play on
 the speakers, I think.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.280
– How many times has this
been played?

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:03.200
It’s one of YouTube’s most 
streamed songs.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.840
– I have no idea.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.000
– Billions of streams.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.240
– It must be hard to hear 
your own song

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:15.480
and not be able to dance,

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.520
but with five people sitting
 like this.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:21.440
– You learned to play the
piano after becoming world-renowned. 

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:22.000
– Yes.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.320
– Why did you do that?

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.640
– When I could make all these
different melodies,

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.960
I felt it wasn’t right.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:39.880
that I could make beautiful 
melodies and songs,

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.480
but couldn’t play them
on the piano.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.760
That was my motivation.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.320
– How did you learn
to play the piano?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.240
– I watched YouTube.

